# expanded/data/v1.hex -- the FROZEN v1 machine-code substrate, as data.
#
# Same [key][len][data] record format and same spelling as data/blob.hex, and
# the same terminating-sentinel convention: the 0 byte is not in the file, the
# reader appends it.  This one is an INPUT, not an output: data/blob.hex is
# generated from the v2 tables, this is the v1 table the v2 blob is built on.
#
# Keys 1-5 are the fixed sections -- 1 prologue, 2 cond, 3 startup, 4 the ELF
# header's non-zero (offset,value) pairs, 5 autoexit -- and every record after
# them is one v1 op byte's machine-code template, keyed by that byte.
#
# This is the whole of what expanded/ used to reach into minimal/boot/golf0.py
# for.  Everything that module exposed is recoverable from these records:
# EPILOGUE is the template for '^', and BASE and FILESZ are p_vaddr and
# p_filesz inside record 4.  boot/v1.py does that reconstruction.
#
# FROZEN.  v1 is frozen (branch `minimal`, tag v1.0-minimal), so this file can
# never legitimately change; .github/workflows/release-minimal.yml re-derives
# it from minimal/tools/mkblob.py on that branch and fails if it differs.
# 23 records, 229 bytes with the sentinel, longest template 46.
